--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.deduct]/2,5 + [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A function template
whose trailing return type is a `decltype` of a CALL containing a pack expansion,
`-> decltype(add(I...))`, is not resolved by CBMC ("found no match for symbol
'impl'"), leaving the call untyped.  A decltype of a fixed-argument call
(`decltype(add(1,2))`) and plain `auto`/`decltype(auto)` forwarding returns are
handled correctly, so the defect is specific to a decltype return type over a
pack-expansion call.  This is the core of cpp17_apply_basic -- libstdc++
std::apply's `__apply_impl` returns `decltype(__invoke(f, get<_Idx>(t)...))` --
and is a separate layer from the std::tuple construction bugs.  g++/clang++
compute r == 3.  Flip to CORE once a decltype-return-type over a pack-expansion
call is resolved.
